      "content": "a small tun (Day 978), a measuring-vessel that contains a quarter of standard measure. The quotes indicate that a quartellus is equivalent to a fourth of a sester or two fifths of a butte (Latham, Dictionary, s.v. quartellus, sextarius)"
    }
